<title>USA: J&amp;L sees new line cutting '97 net $0.30-0.35.</title>
<headline>J&amp;L sees new line cutting '97 net $0.30-0.35.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>J&amp;L Specialty Steel Inc said Monday it expected the start-up of a direct roll anneal and pickle line at its Midland, Pa., stainless steel plant to reduce its 1997 net income by between $0.30 and $0.35 per share.</p>
<p>The line is to be completed in December, with full production expected by the end of 1997.</p>
<p>The company said the financial impact of the new line would be felt primarily in the second, third and fourth quarters of 1997.</p>
</text>
